      "score": false,
      "model_answer": "The polynomial P(x) = (1+x+x^2+...+x^17)^2 - x^17 can be factored as:\n\nP(x) = (1+x+...+x^18)(1+x+...+x^16)\n\nThis can be rewritten using geometric series formulas:\nP(x) = [(x^19 - 1)/(x-1)] × [(x^17 - 1)/(x-1)]\n\nThe roots of P(x) = 0 are:\n- The 19th roots of unity (except x=1): e^(2πik/19) for k = 1, 2, ..., 18 → 18 roots\n- The 17th roots of unity (except x=1): e^(2πik/17) for k = 1, 2, ..., 16 → 16 roots\n\nSince gcd(19, 17) = 1, these two sets of roots are disjoint (the only common root would be x=1, which is excluded).\n\nTotal roots: 18 + 16 = 34\n\nAll roots of unity have absolute value |x| = 1, so all 34 roots of P(x) lie on the unit circle.\n\nThe answer is 34.",
